# Copy to services/.env. Two lines, and only the first of them is a secret.

# The one password, checked as HTTP Basic with the user name "admin". It guards the settings
# page and the VNC screen alike: the RFB port itself listens on loopback inside the container
# and the only route to it is /vnc/, which is behind this. The container refuses to start
# without one. Everything else is set on the settings page.
VNC_PASSWORD=

# Which host port the container's single port lands on. The roster, the tiles, the settings
# page and the sign-in screen are all paths under it, so this is the only one to route:
#
#   /v1/people              the panel's people-url        no password
#   /tiles/{z}/{x}/{y}.png  the panel's map-tile-url      no password
#   /health                                               no password
#   /                       the settings page             password
#   /vnc/                   the sign-in screen            password
#
# Point one name at it. Two things the reverse proxy in front has to do: allow a websocket
# upgrade under /vnc/ with a read timeout in the hours rather than the seconds, and terminate
# TLS with a certificate the panel's system trust store already knows - it rejects rather than
# prompts, and it does not follow redirects.
HOST_PORT=8087
